*Solution Steps Walkthrough:*

1. Identify the boundary circle points on the imaginary axis: $z = 3 i$ and $z = -i$.
2. Place the pole on the boundary to map the circle to a straight line (the real axis).
3. Use the symmetry of the imaginary axis to constrain the form of $T(z)$.
4. Enforce the fixed point condition $T(i) = i$ to determine the multiplicative constant.
